// @name: Synth saw — basic
// @tagline: single `new synth saw` voice — must sound with zero external assets
// @description: The smallest Mercury patch that produces sound: one sawtooth synth voice on a
//   repeating time grid, shaped with an envelope. Adapted from the "Evaluate a mercury code file"
//   usage snippet in the mercury-engine README (synth line only, sample lines stripped — this
//   file is the SYNTH half of that example, on purpose: it does not touch the sample set at all).
// @language: mercury
// @outputs: audio
// @level: didactic
// @tags: mercury, ab-corpus, synth, no-samples
// @source: https://github.com/tmhglnd/mercury-engine/blob/main/README.md#resume-evaluate-and-silence
//
// A/B — mercury — Synth saw (basic). Original: https://github.com/tmhglnd/mercury-engine/blob/main/README.md
// Coller/évaluer la voix, puis comparer au rendu de l'outil original (mercury.timohoogland.com).
// Test de robustesse : synthèse pure — DOIT sonner même si le jeu de samples n'est pas chargé.

@core
@tempo:120

@actor v  eval.mercury  transport.audio

S -> v

v -> `new synth saw note(0 0) time(1/16) shape(1 80)`:4
